 Messages exist in English (`en`) and Korean (`ko`), in
 `src/i18n/messages.js`. The server answers in `LARDER_LANG` (default `en`).
+
+## Sales and variance
+
+- `POST /import/sales` accepts a JSON object with a `csv` string containing
+  `ticket,soldAt,dishId,qty`. The ticket must be nonempty, `soldAt` must be
+  an ISO 8601 timestamp with a UTC offset or `Z`, and `dishId` and `qty`
+  must be positive whole numbers. Multiple lines can share a ticket.
+  Previously imported tickets are skipped. A successful response contains
+  `tickets` (new unique tickets) and `dishes` (the sum of their quantities).
+  An invalid row or insufficient stock rejects the entire upload and the
+  error identifies the CSV row.
+- `GET /reports/variance?from=YYYY-MM-DD&to=YYYY-MM-DD` returns an array
+  sorted by `itemId`. Each entry has `itemId`, `theoretical`, `actual`,
+  and `variance` (actual minus theoretical) in the item's unit. The range
+  includes both UTC dates. Theoretical use comes from sales by `soldAt`
+  and actual use from all consume movements by their ledger timestamp.
+  Only items with positive theoretical or actual use appear.
